; =============================================================================
; P2-EC32MB module netlist (whole-module, all 8 schematic pages merged)
; =============================================================================
; Source        : Parallax "Propeller 2 Edge Module with 32MB RAM" schematic
;                 File     : P2-EC32MB-RevB-SCHEMATIC.pdf (8 pages)
;                 Part No. : P2-EC32MB    Revision: B    Last Update: 29 Mar 2022 (MM)
;                 Downloaded from parallax.com (P2 Edge Module with 32 MB RAM,
;                 product downloads).
; License       : Copyright 2022 Parallax Incorporated. Open Source Hardware,
;                 Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
;                 (CC BY-SA 4.0), http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0
;                 Attribution: Parallax Inc., 599 Menlo Drive, Rocklin, CA 95765.
; Transcribed   : 2026-07-19, manual transcription from the vendor PDF
;                 (8 per-page transcriptions merged; every flagged ambiguity
;                 re-verified against 300 dpi renders; values and MPNs verified
;                 against the BOM on schematic page 8 and the product guide).
; STATIC ARTIFACT - never regenerated. The vendor schematic is the source of
; truth; regenerate this file only on a vendor revision change (Rev B today).
;
; Conventions
; - Format: KiCad netlist-export s-expression dialect, (export (version "E")).
; - J203 (80-way card edge, the consumer-facing surface): pin numbers are the
;   edge finger numbers 1..80; the printed edge label is the pinfunction.
;   Fingers 1-40 = Module Front (pin 1 marked), 41-80 = Module Back.
; - U100 (P2X8C4M64P): the schematic prints no package pad numbers, so pin ids
;   are the printed pin NAMES, with U100 I/O ids normalized to uniform P0..P63
;   VDD, GND, TEST, RESN, XI, XO). The 16 identically-named VDD pins are
;   collapsed into the single logical node (pin "VDD"); the symbol draws one
;   GND pin. TEST is a separate pin, tied to the GND net.
; - All other ICs likewise use pin names as pin ids (no pad numbers printed).
;   Active-low overbars are rendered KiCad-style in pinfunction (~{CS}) with
;   ASCII-safe pin ids (CSn). Slashed names use "_" in the id (DO(IO1) ->
;   DO_IO1, CMD/MOSI -> CMD_MOSI, NC/GND -> NC_GND, GND-P -> GND_P).
; - U401 (reverse-polarity P-FET): the symbol draws four joined drain fingers;
;   they are collapsed into the single node (pin "D").
; - S301 pin ids: <position>_<OFF|ON> (1:LED ENABLE, 2:FLASH, 3:P59 pull-up,
;   4:P59 pull-down); closing a switch connects its OFF-side net to its
;   ON-side net.
; - Passives use positional pins "1"/"2" (no numbering printed): pin 1 = the
;   rail/label side, pin 2 = the ground-symbol side, as noted per transcription.
; - LEDs: A = anode, K = cathode.
; - Unlabeled local wires use KiCad-style synthetic names: Net-(REF-PIN).
; - No-connects (no nodes emitted): J203 fingers 55, 56, 59-67, 69-77
;   (P57/LED, P56/LED, P48-P55, V48, P40-P47, V40 - unused on this module,
;   those P2 pins serve the PSRAMs/LEDs on-board); J301 SW1, SW2, DAT1, DAT2;
;   U402.EN and U403.EN (vendor note: "EN NC = Default 2.5ms startup").
;   XTAL_XO is a labeled single-node net (P2 XO unused with the external TCXO).
; - BOM-only RefDes: PCB (raw board, no nodes) and NC_Net (layout node, one
;   node on net NC_Net); J701/J702 are the mounting holes, tied to GND.
;
; Resolutions made while merging (verified on 300 dpi re-reads of the PDF):
; 1. VIO rail naming: pages 1, 2 and the page-5 cap bank print zero-padded
;    VIO_00_07 / VIO_08_15; only the page-5 LDO output arrows print VIO_0_7 /
;    VIO_8_15. Same electrical rail (vendor label inconsistency) - unified
;    here as VIO_00_07 / VIO_08_15.
; 2. LED buffer (page 6): U601 74LVC2G04 inputs are 1A = P2_IO38, 2A =
;    P2_IO39; outputs sink the LED cathodes (D601 K to 1Y, D602 K to 2Y); the
;    two anodes join one node into R601 (1K) whose far side is DIPSW_LEDPWR
;    (LED supply gated by S301 pos 1 from Common_LDOin). Vendor note: LEDs
;    turn ON when the P2_IO pin asserts high. U601 Vcc = Common_LDOin.
; 3. Net spelling DIPSW_LEDPWR confirmed on both page 3 and page 6 (an
;    earlier brief said DPSW_LEDPWR - wrong).
; 4. MPNs taken from the page-8 BOM (not printed on the circuit pages):
;    U100 P2X8C4M64P; U101/U601 NXP 74LVC2G04GW,125; U301 Winbond
;    W25Q128JVSIM TR; U302-U305 AP Memory APS6404L-3SQR-ZR; U401 Vishay
;    SI3417DV-T1-GE3; U402/U403 Diodes Inc AP62301Z6-7; U404 STMicro
;    STM1061N16WX6F; U501-U508 OnSemi NCP114AMX330TCG; X100 EPSON TG2520SMN
;    20.0000M-ECGNNM3; C132 Samsung CL05B102KO5NNNC; D601/D602 Inolux
;    IN-S63AS5UW; L401/L402 Pulse PA5430.332NLT; J301 Molex 473092651.
; 5. PSRAM NC(EP) ties confirmed asymmetric per vendor routing note: U302 ->
;    VIO_48_55, U304 -> VIO_40_47, U303/U305 -> GND.
; 6. Oscillator topology (page 1): TCXO OUT -> C132 -> [2A->2Y inverter with
;    R101 100K feedback] -> [1A->1Y] -> XTAL_XI; the 2Y/R101 vertical wire
;    crosses the 1Y wire WITHOUT a junction dot (verified at high zoom), so
;    1Y drives only XTAL_XI. U101 Vcc = VIO_24_31.
; 7. R601 printed 1K on page 6; BOM groups R201, R601 as 1K 5% - consistent.
; 8. Page-6 note "Bypass cap with Cxxx" names no real RefDes; no such cap
;    exists in the BOM - nothing emitted.
; 9. Reset chain unified across pages 2 and 4: J203 finger 46 (RESn) -> R201
;    1K -> P2_RESN; R100 10.5K pull-up to VIO_56_63; U404 ~OUT (brownout
;    detector on Common_VDD) also drives P2_RESN.
; =============================================================================

; =============================================================================
; embsim-board fixture note (appended; the vendor provenance above is verbatim)
; =============================================================================
; Role in this repo
;   The netlist reference for a board whose export carries NO (libsource ...)
;   entries - it was transcribed from a PDF, not exported by an EDA tool. That
;   makes it the fixture for PartRegistry's reference-designator classification
;   fallback (classify_unnamed_by_reference): with no part names to key on, the
;   85 passives classify from their R/C/L/D prefixes and the five J-prefixed
;   pad/socket symbols become board boundaries, leaving only the module's active
;   silicon for the registry.
;   It is also the mating half of mad_edge.net: both netlists number the 80-way
;   card edge by FINGER number, so the module's J203 fingers and the EdgeBoard's
;   J3 socket pins correspond 1:1 (see board/tests/machine_parts/mod.rs).
; Consumers
;   board/tests/ec32mb_module.rs   - the module as a Board
;   board/tests/machine_system.rs  - the module inside the whole machine
; STATIC ARTIFACT - never regenerated from an EDA tool (see above). Update only
; on a vendor revision change, by re-transcribing from the vendor schematic.
; =============================================================================

(export (version "E")
  (design
    (source "P2-EC32MB-RevB-SCHEMATIC.pdf (Parallax P2-EC32MB Rev B, 29 Mar 2022)")
    (date "2026-07-19")
